WEBVTT

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:49.240
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: ...of the impeachment court.

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:45.920
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: The Sergeant at Arms directed to make a proclamation.

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:56.820
Alfredo Sotto Corpuz: All persons are commanded to keep silent under pain of penalty while the impeachment court is in session for the trial of Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte.

00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:06.220
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: The impeachment trial of Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte is hereby called to order. We shall be led in prayer by Senator Judge Pia Cayetano.

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:17.970
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: Let us bow our heads. Almighty God, we come before you today seeking your wisdom and guidance as we carry our duties.

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:19.670
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: We

00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:50.790
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: lift up to you every Filipino family, especially those struggling with rising cost of living, those affected by calamities, and those facing uncertainty about their future. Grant us wisdom to make sound decisions, humility to listen, courage to do what is right, and compassion for those whose voices are often unheard. Remind us that beyond our differences, we share a common purpose to serve our country, protect the welfare of our people, and build a better future for every Filipino. We entrust our nation and our people to your loving care. In Jesus' name we pray. Amen.

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:51.330
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Amen.

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:53.970
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: The Clerk of Court will now call the roll.

00:07:55.630 --> 00:07:57.590
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: Roll call of members. Senator Judge Aquino.

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:39.090
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: Sen. Judge Cayetano Alan, Sen. Judge Cayetano Pia, Sen. Judge De La Rosa, Sen. Judge Ejercito, Sen. Judge Estrada, Sen. Judge Go, Sen. Judge Hontiveros, Sen. Judge Lacson, Sen. Judge Lapid, Sen. Judge Legarda, Sen. Judge Marcoleta, Sen. Judge Marcos, Sen. Judge Padilla, Sen. Judge Pangilinan, Sen. Judge Sotto III, Sen. Judge Tulfo Erwin, Sen. Judge Tulfo Raffy, Senator Judge Villanueva, Senator Judge Villar Camille, Senator Judge Villar Mark, Senator Judge Zubiri, The Presiding Officer, Senator Judge Escudero, The Senate President, Senator Judge Gatchalian.

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:43.830
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: With 13 Senator Judges present, the Chair declares the presence of a quorum.

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:56.490
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: In accordance with the rules of procedure on impeachment trials, the Chair now recognizes the duly presiding officer to preside over the proceedings of the impeachment court.

00:08:57.810 --> 00:09:08.940
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Mr. Senate President. If there are no objections, we shall dispense with the reading of the November 10, 2026 Journal of the Senate, sitting as an impeachment court, and consider the same as approved.

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:13.560
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: The clerk will please call the case before the impeachment court.

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:19.900
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: Case number 004-2026 in the matter of impeachment trial of Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte.

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:22.520
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Appearances of the parties.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:27.480
Rep. Terry L. Ridon: Magandang umaga po. Same appearances for the prosecution, Your Honor.

00:09:27.950 --> 00:09:30.990
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Atty. Ridon, who will handle the next witness?

00:09:32.410 --> 00:09:35.450
Rep. Terry L. Ridon: Depends on the next witness, Your Honor.

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:37.230
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: The next witness is Atty. Punay.

00:09:37.230 --> 00:09:39.010
Rep. Terry L. Ridon: It will be Atty. Kapunan.

00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:40.640
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: In

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:45.400
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: that case, Atty. Kapunan, good morning. Atty. Sheila, appearances for the respondent.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:58.380
Atty. Sheila C. Sison: Good morning, Your Honor. Same appearance for the respondent accused. I will ask the court to acknowledge Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular for the examination of our witness, Atty. Balucanag Punay.

00:09:59.730 --> 00:10:01.070
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Atty. Justin, good morning.

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:01.790
Atty. Sheila C. Sison: Thank you.

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:09.840
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: And again, good morning, Atty. Lorna. Kindly call your witness, Atty. Justin.

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:10.320
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Good

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:19.600
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: morning, Your Honor. Thank you. For the next witness, Your Honor, may we respectfully call to the witness stand, Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay, Your Honor.

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:39.850
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay is hereby directed to situate herself with the assistance of the Secretariat to the witness stand. As soon as she is so situated, the clerk is directed to administer the oath. After the oath, Attorney Justin.

00:10:42.730 --> 00:10:58.000
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: Ma'am, please raise your right hand. You, Suzette Balucanag-Punay, do swear that the evidence you shall give in the case now pending between the Philippines and Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte shall be the truth, the whole truth, and nothing but the truth. So help you God.

00:10:58.340 --> 00:10:58.700
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I do.

00:11:00.980 --> 00:11:10.540
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kindly sit down, Attorney Suzette. Atty. Suzette, naunawaan niyo po ay inyong pinanumpaan kaugnay sa pagbibigay niyo ng inyong testimonya sa hukumang ito?

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:11.660
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, Your Honor.

00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:17.620
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, ma'am. And good morning, ma'am. Yes, Atty. Justin, what is it? May I proceed? I

00:11:17.620 --> 00:11:20.140
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: was actually going to ask for the flashing of the purposes.

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:23.680
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes, kindly make your offer, Atty. Justin.

00:11:23.880 --> 00:12:18.250
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Thank you, Your Honor. We'll proceed, Your Honor. Good morning, Your Honor. We are offering the testimony of our next witness, Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay for the following purposes. Number one, to prove that she is the in-house counsel of both GenCorp Industries Inc. and Metro City Chow Foods Corporation. Number two, to prove that GenCorp Industries Inc. and Metro City Chow Foods Corporation are duly organized and existing domestic corporations under Philippine law. and that they are legally engaged in the operation of fast food restaurant chains pursuant to their respective franchise agreements with Jollibee and Chowking respectively. Number three,

00:12:20.500 --> 00:13:00.840
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: may we request the tech to flash the next slide. Thank you. To prove that the vice president is neither a stockholder, officer, director, of GenCorp Industries Inc., and that she made no capital contribution to the corporation or its Jollibee franchise operations, and that, contrary to the findings of Attorney Alexander B. Cabrera in his reported forensic report, she, and I'm referring to the Vice President, has no ownership or equity interest in said corporation. Number four,

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:01.720
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: to

00:13:01.720 --> 00:14:03.920
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: prove. The factual inaccuracies and errors specifically in respect to Table 39 of the purported forensic report supposedly prepared by Attorney Alexander B. Cabrera, particularly his computation of the Vice President's purported total undeclared income from GenCorp Industries Inc. and that the same is unsupported by the corporate records and does not accurately reflect The actual income attributable to the Vice President from GenCorp Industries, Inc. Number 5. To prove that the Vice President exercises no control over, no participation in, or supervisory role over the management and business operations of GenCorp Industries, Inc. or in any of its contracts with the government. Number 6.

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:09.980
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: To prove the true nature of the Vice President's interest in GenCorp Industries, Inc.

00:14:10.880 --> 00:14:13.300
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Number seven.

00:14:13.300 --> 00:15:07.980
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: To prove that, although the Vice President is a stockholder of record and is listed as a director and a member of the Compensation Committee of Metro City Chow Foods Corporation, she has neither participated in nor exercised the functions, duties, and responsibilities pertaining to these positions and that she exercises no control over nor does she participate in or supervise the management and operations of the corporation. And number eight, finally, to disprove and controvert the material allegations under Article 2 of the Articles of Impeachment and the Forensic Report supposed. Atty. Alexander B. Cabrera, to identify documents and other matters related to the foregoing, Your Honor.

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:11.120
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Comment, Attorney Lorna.

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:12.440
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Good morning, Your Honors.

00:15:12.560 --> 00:15:15.400
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Good morning again.

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:16.820
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Good morning, Counsel. Good morning, Attorney. Good morning.

00:15:16.820 --> 00:15:18.240
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Good morning, Attorney Lorna.

00:15:19.580 --> 00:15:33.100
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: A comment on the offer of purpose for which this witness is being presented, Your Honor. On the first your honor, offer,

00:15:33.100 --> 00:16:28.700
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: The Counsel for Defense mentions that this witness is in-house counsel. Not a comment, Your Honor, but may we be clarified because she is being presented as in-house counsel of both Metro Company and GenCorp. May we know from counsel, Madam, Mr. Presiding Officer, can the Presiding Officer please inquire from counsel? or the witness herself, if she is authorized by virtue of any board resolution from any or both of these companies to testify in today's hearing, Your Honor. To us, this is very important because otherwise, if she is not duly authorized by a board resolution from both companies, we will question her capacity.

00:16:30.840 --> 00:17:12.300
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: capacity to even appear before this honorable tribunal and more so to testify on behalf of both companies absent a duly authorized board certificate, a secretary certificate from both companies specifically indicating that she is authorized not only to represent the company, both companies, but to appear today in this impeachment trial, and not only to appear and testify, but to identify documents pertaining to these two companies, Your Honor.

00:17:12.540 --> 00:17:16.020
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: What is your basis, Attorney Lorna, in asking for a board resolution?

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:53.460
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Yes, Your Honor, because we all know we're all... The board resolution is important because we do not want... This is not to preempt the testimony of the witness, Your Honor, but we do not want at some point in time that she will call to the attention of the honorable presiding officer or hide behind the lawyer-client privilege, Your Honor.

00:17:56.240 --> 00:19:05.150
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Yes, Your Honor. Just a brief response, of course. Respectful response to the point raised by the good counsel of the prosecution. First, Your Honor, her appearance today is by virtue of a subpoena, Your Honor. In other words, her appearance today is in compliance with the authority of this honorable court. And number two, Your Honor, I think we need to record that a lawyer has an implied authority to represent the client. But in any case, Your Honor, if the concerns of... The good counsel from the prosecution is to hide behind supposedly the veil of lawyer-client privilege. It is, number one, a premature objection. Number two, it is not an objection that she is entitled to raise and only the corporate clients can raise that. But number three, Your Honor, in any case, the witness will be under oath in respect to her answers, Your Honor. And finally, Your Honor, I would just like to point for the record and it is best for us to recall. When the bank representatives were being presented who represented corporations by virtue of subpoena, no issue with respect to authority was ever raised. That is all, Your Honor.

00:19:05.450 --> 00:21:29.390
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Your Honor, please, on the last point, with reference to the bank officials, Your Honor, as regards their authority to represent the banks upon a subpoena by this honorable court, Your Honor, It was up to the defense to question the authority of these bank representatives to appear and testify. They did not do so, Your Honor. We are not presuming, Your Honor, the same. We want to know whether this witness really is qualified because she is neither in the general information sheets Her name is not there. And that is why she is being presented today. She is also not in the financial statements of both companies. And that is why she is being presented here today. She also, Your Honor, on the third point, she also, Your Honor, Her name does not appear as well in the articles of incorporation. And that is why when counsel says that she is in-house counsel, it is very important that we have on record a written board resolution authorizing her to appear and testify on behalf. Because even if she is summoned by virtue of subpoena, It does not behood, it may not be a complete authority for her to testify here because she can claim or the companies that she represents here may claim that whatever facts or whatever documents she identifies here is without authority of these companies, Your Honor. And that is why. Just to shorten this proceedings, Your Honor, because this is only the first item in this offer of testimony, Your Honor. May we ask from counsel, in any event, Mr. Presiding Officer, that at some point within the day or within this week, Your Honor, that they present to this honorable Presiding Officer a board resolution or a...

00:21:30.990 --> 00:21:46.010
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Secretary Certificate affirming her authority to come and speak for the companies, both companies, and to identify records for the companies, Your Honor. May we reserve that

00:21:46.010 --> 00:21:46.250
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: right?

00:21:46.470 --> 00:22:21.920
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: For the meantime, the court will note the... Query and the answer of the counsel for respondent. And kindly continue with your comment on the offer, Attorney Lorna. And the court will make a ruling at the appropriate time, either before we begin after hearing your entire comment and offer, or once the appropriate question has been asked and the objection would come into play once we cross that bridge. So in the meantime, kindly continue with your other comments, if any, to the offer of Attorney Justin.

00:22:22.240 --> 00:22:44.380
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: We submit, Your Honor. On the second offer, Your Honor, as regards an offer to the effect that GenCorp and Metro Company are duly organized and existing and legally engaged to conduct business for fast food activities, Your Honor, we will stipulate.

00:22:47.070 --> 00:22:48.390
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: As to the second offer.

00:22:48.720 --> 00:22:56.480
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: As to the second offer, Your Honor, as to the due legal existence of Gen. Cor. and Metro.

00:22:58.520 --> 00:23:02.560
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: May we proceed, Your Honor?

00:23:02.780 --> 00:23:04.200
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: As to

00:23:04.200 --> 00:23:23.780
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: the third offer, that statement that the Vice President is neither stockholder, director of Gen. Cor. Inc., No capital contribution. Subject to cross-examination, Your Honor.

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:37.670
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: On offer number four, as regards the factual table, table 39, with reference to the forensic computation of prosecutors'

00:23:39.800 --> 00:24:03.190
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: expert witness, Your Honor. Subject to cross-examination. As well as offer number five, as regards to a statement by counsel, that the Vice President does not exercise any control, participation, or nor any supervision in GenCorp, Your Honor. Subject to cross-examination.

00:24:05.400 --> 00:24:11.430
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Number six, Your Honor, the nature of her interest in both companies.

00:24:13.230 --> 00:24:35.290
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Subject to cross-examination. And number seven, to prove that she has no control, the Vice President, over Metro Company, Your Honor. Again, this is subject to cross-examination. And lastly, their blanket offer as to the forensic report submitted by

00:24:35.290 --> 00:24:39.490
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Prosecutor's Forensic Expert, Attorney Cabrera, Your Honor.

00:24:39.750 --> 00:24:41.290
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Subject to cross-examination.

00:24:44.070 --> 00:25:41.750
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Court will make a ruling on the first one. The court will in the meantime allow the testimony of attorney Punay on her oath as a lawyer upon which she owes candor and fidelity not only to the regular courts but to this court as well. And although corporations cannot act on its own, We as of yet do not know, based on that testimony, if she will be testifying on behalf of the corporation or only about the corporation. But my presumption, Attorney Justin, is given that she is here appearing as in-house counsel of the corporation, that's the corporations, the two corporations. That she waives any privilege in regard to lawyer-client privilege as regards the two corporations, not necessarily the individual stockholders. Would that be correct?

00:25:42.170 --> 00:25:53.030
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Your Honor, unfortunately, as a co-lawyer myself, I cannot answer that question, Your Honor. I think it is best to ask the witness herself with respect to that. At the proper time.

00:25:53.170 --> 00:25:53.490
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: At

00:25:53.490 --> 00:26:25.160
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: the proper time, counsel. If and when she invokes it. With a reminder, Attorney Punay, that again, Once you testify as to the two corporations, it would be unfair for you not to invoke the privilege for anything that will favor one side and to invoke the privilege should the question now pertain to evidence you may give against the same side. With that caveat and reminder, the court will allow it. Attorney, Senator Judge Pangalinan is recognized. What is your pleasure, sir?

00:26:29.960 --> 00:27:00.450
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Just a clarification. On the status of this next witness, I recall, Mr. Presiding Officer, that when Attorney Poa took the witness stand in the previous articles, at some point he was a witness and yet he was also lawyer for the respondent and invoked lawyer-client privilege.

00:27:02.820 --> 00:27:22.270
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: and refused to answer questions from the senator judges. So, following that precedent, do we expect this witness to likewise invoke that privilege as it has been done by previous witnesses?

00:27:23.270 --> 00:27:24.030
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: I

00:27:24.030 --> 00:28:03.270
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: ask this because it would quickly speed up matters if... As earlier raised, that he has been authorized by his clients. He's the in-house counsel of GenCorp and of MetroChao. It would have been simpler if both corporations agreed for their general counsel to testify here and waive lawyer-client privilege. It will save us all a lot of time. So, I'd like that clarified, Mr.

00:28:05.410 --> 00:28:06.510
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Presiding Officer.

00:28:06.590 --> 00:29:07.740
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Senator Judge Kiko. Part of the Chair's ruling is that we are presuming, as I said earlier, that she appeared here with the proper authorization on her oath and candor she owes to the Court as an officer of the Court and as a member of the Bar, and that her appearance here is duly authorized, and that Privilege if any between her and the corporation she will be testifying to has been waived by the client and that she cannot choose when to invoke privilege and when not to invoke privilege as to these two clients of hers, the companies. Without prejudice, Atty. Punay, to claiming privilege to the individual shareholders that you may independently have knowledge about as a lawyer. which can be covered by privilege and which we will not compel you to testify in regard to them individually, separately from the companies. Is that understood, Attorney Pune?

00:29:07.860 --> 00:29:08.660
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, Your Honor.

00:29:11.350 --> 00:29:13.630
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kindly turn on the mic of Senator Judge Kiko.

00:29:14.010 --> 00:29:21.630
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: With the response of the witness, we can proceed. Thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer.

00:29:21.770 --> 00:29:24.970
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Senator Judge Kiko. You may proceed, Attorney Justin, with your direct examination.

00:29:25.530 --> 00:29:26.010
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Thank

00:29:26.010 --> 00:29:26.510
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: you, Your Honor.

00:29:29.640 --> 00:29:40.140
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Noting the stipulation of the counsel for the prosecutor as to the fact that GenCorp owns several franchises of Jollibee.

00:29:40.700 --> 00:29:49.600
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Yes, Your Honor. We'll keep it in mind. Thank you. Proceeding to my direct examination, Your Honor. Atty. Suzette, maayong buntag.

00:29:49.920 --> 00:29:50.780
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Good morning.

00:29:51.560 --> 00:29:58.580
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: For the record, Atty. Suzette, can you please state your name, age, and address to this impeachment court?

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:10.100
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Balucanag, Punay, 41 years old. And my office address is 3rd floor, PVL Building, Rizal Street, Corner, Bolton Street, Davao City.

00:30:11.000 --> 00:30:17.740
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Atty. Suzette, apologies if I have to ask this. What is your profession, if any, Atty. Suzette?

00:30:18.060 --> 00:30:18.880
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I'm a lawyer.

00:30:19.280 --> 00:30:22.140
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: And how many years have you been a lawyer, for the record?

00:30:23.120 --> 00:30:24.380
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: 15 years now.

00:30:26.020 --> 00:30:33.100
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Now, Atty. Suzette, you are here in the impeachment court right now. Can you please tell us what you know about this case, if anything at all?

00:30:34.460 --> 00:30:38.560
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: This is the impeachment against Vice President Sara Duterte.

00:30:39.440 --> 00:30:54.820
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: And given that this is the impeachment case against the Vice President, Sara Zimmerman Duterte, can you please tell us what relationship, whether professional or personal, do you have with the Vice President, if anything?

00:30:55.860 --> 00:31:00.800
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I have no personal or professional relationship with the Vice President.

00:31:01.190 --> 00:31:03.310
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: In that case, how do you know the Vice President?

00:31:04.390 --> 00:31:09.890
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I am from Davao City, so she was a Mayor and Vice Mayor before.

00:31:10.430 --> 00:31:20.810
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Sinabi niyo kanina, Atty., na aware po kayo ng impeachment case ito ng Vice Presidente. How are you made aware of this impeachment proceeding, if you can recall or if you know?

00:31:21.870 --> 00:31:24.430
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: It's all over social media.

00:31:25.790 --> 00:31:29.080
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: And Atty. Suzette? Why are you here today?

00:31:30.100 --> 00:31:33.420
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: By virtue of a subpoena issued to me by the Senate.

00:31:33.940 --> 00:31:43.120
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Okay. Atty. Suzette, what companies are you connected to in relation to this impeachment trial, if you can remember?

00:31:43.970 --> 00:31:49.670
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I am with GenCorp Industries, Inc. and Metro City Chow Foods Corporation.

00:31:51.960 --> 00:32:06.540
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Okay. Punahin po natin sinabi niyo po na GenCorp Industries, Inc. May question po. You mentioned that you are with GenCorp Industries, Inc. What is your position in GenCorp Industries, Inc., kung mayroon man?

00:32:06.680 --> 00:32:08.620
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I am their in-house counsel.

00:32:09.120 --> 00:32:18.540
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: And as the in-house counsel of GenCorp Industries, Inc., can you please kindly tell us all what your duties and responsibilities are in said corporation?

00:32:19.410 --> 00:32:35.970
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: As in-house counsel, I manage all of their legal inquiries. I also do, I assist them in litigation. I do investigation for employee discipline and I have access to their corporate records.

00:32:36.570 --> 00:32:42.350
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Okay. And can you please tell everyone when you started working for GenCorp Industries Inc po?

00:32:42.590 --> 00:32:44.930
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: In 2022, mid of 2022.

00:32:45.470 --> 00:32:49.670
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: And before that, san po kayo nagtatrabaho kung pwede pong may tanong?

00:32:50.300 --> 00:32:53.820
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Before, I was with PhilHealth before.

00:32:55.020 --> 00:33:01.430
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: And by PhilHealth, ito po ba yung government institution po? Just a clarification.

00:33:02.010 --> 00:33:02.550
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, sir.

00:33:02.730 --> 00:33:10.510
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Now, for the record, can you please tell us what you know about, what is GenCorp Industries, Inc.?

00:33:10.830 --> 00:33:17.690
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: GenCorp Industries, Inc. is a domestic corporation and its line of business is in the fast food industry.

00:33:19.140 --> 00:33:31.300
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Sinabi niyo po na domestic corporation po itong GenCorp Industries, Inc. My question is, where's the principal address or office address of this GenCorp Industries, Inc.? Kung alam niyo po.

00:33:33.960 --> 00:33:40.100
