Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Your Honor, however, please allow me to speak.

05:07:03.830 --> 05:07:04.730
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes, Attorney Justice.

05:07:04.730 --> 05:07:40.720
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Your Honor, again, our witnesses here are entitled to rights. One of those rights is not to be badgered by questions. Only this impeachment court will resolve in the final decision it will make. Because what Attorney Capunan is asking the witnesses, isn't this a constitutional violation? But at the start of this hearing, we are all aware as lawyers, Attorney, that only the respective senator-judges can make. That final determination. We ask, Your Honor, that this is clearly already badgering the witness as Atty. Lorna Caponan, with all due respect, knows what she is doing, Your Honor. May we move on?

05:07:41.160 --> 05:09:04.490
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: I also know, Your Honor, what counsel is doing. Counsel is manifesting that I am badgering. I may have a loud voice, Your Honor, but this is already my tame voice. It could be louder. In fact, this is my kind voice. When I ask the witness, Your Honor, if she knows. Because she should know. Fifteen years in the practice of law, you do not know what should not be declared and what should be declared as a public officer. You do not know that a public officer cannot receive income apart from her legitimate salary from any other business or exercise of any profession. And to answer, Your Honor, That she prefers not to answer, I think is a violation of her oath as a lawyer. And that's why I feel agitated, Your Honor. It's a violation of her oath of office that she will say, I prefer not to answer. As an officer of the court, especially a highest impeachment court, to say that, Your Honor, I think that should be... That should not be accepted as an answer, Your Honor. I am badgering, Your Honor. I have the right to badger. We have the right to badger a witness who does not want to answer a question that should be answered.

05:09:05.210 --> 05:09:17.050
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Forgive me, counsel. Even if she refused to answer, no counsel has the right to badger the witness still, although you can be frustrated or disappointed. However,

05:09:18.710 --> 05:09:41.160
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: The witness already answered that she does not know after the court reminded her that she cannot refuse to answer the question. And she already changed her answer and said she does not know. You have made your point, counsel. You have spread into the records your theory. Move on to your next point, Attorney Lorna.

05:09:41.560 --> 05:09:44.580
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Let us now go to Metro.

