05:17:28.260 --> 05:17:29.300
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Is that? Okay.

05:17:29.620 --> 05:17:41.900
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Earlier you said that both the Vice President and Jaime D. Cruz have interest in Metro.

05:17:42.380 --> 05:17:43.260
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, ma'am.

05:17:43.380 --> 05:18:19.000
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: But in GenCorp, it is only Jaime D. Cruz that has interest. And yet, in the GIS, General Information Sheet, and yet the Vice President declared. Inursal, and that she is a shareholder. I point your attention now, and if you could read for the record, what is stated here amongst the forensic findings of expert witness, Attorney Cabrera.

05:18:20.780 --> 05:18:24.760
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Would you like to read it or would you like me to read it? Ako na lang.

05:18:26.510 --> 05:21:10.580
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Okay. May I point the court, Your Honor, to the last paragraph? In page 22, it says, it is possible, and this is Attorney Cabrera speaking, it is possible, in my professional opinion, that the reason why the GIS of GenCorp did not disclose the respondent as stockholder is to avoid a documented conflict of interest issue, i.e., the city of Davao. dealing with a corporation owned by a family member which in this case is a previous mayor and current vice president. Note that a conflict of interest blatantly violates bidding rules. In Respondent's non-disclosure of her stockholdings in the GIS of GenCorp, notwithstanding her voluntary declaration of business interest in her salient, may feign an appearance of legitimacy that enables GenCorp to participate in public bidding processes in Davao City. In fact, In the recent testimony of current Mayor Sebastian Duterte, GENCORS secured 19 government contracts with the City of Davao, with her said brother Mayor Sebastian Duterte serving as head of the procurement entity or HOPE. Finally, If I may continue, based on our review of the GIS of GenCorp, we also found that it was JTC group of companies that was indicated as GenCorp's ultimate beneficial owner. This is not compliant with SEC Memorandum Beneficial Ownership Disclosure Framework which requires disclosure. of the identity of the natural person who ultimately owns, controls, or exercises effective control over reporting entity. Okay, my point, my question to you, Madam Witness, is you confirmed earlier on direct examination that GenCorp has government contracts with the City of Davao, correct?

05:21:11.050 --> 05:21:11.730
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, ma'am.

05:21:11.830 --> 05:21:18.030
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: And 19 government contracts, not only with the city of Davao, but with PhilHealth.

05:21:18.510 --> 05:21:19.470
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, ma'am.

05:21:19.770 --> 05:21:24.270
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Incidentally, you are connected with PhilHealth Davao?

05:21:25.230 --> 05:21:27.110
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Until 2019 only.

05:21:27.550 --> 05:21:31.590
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Until 2019. But you

05:21:33.260 --> 05:21:34.960
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: joined. When did you join GenCorp?

05:21:35.480 --> 05:21:36.240
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: 2022.

05:21:36.900 --> 05:21:40.530
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: So, how long were you in PhilHealth?

05:21:41.070 --> 05:21:42.590
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Five years from 2014.

05:21:43.320 --> 05:21:48.940
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: So you were in PhilHealth for five years and then you went to GenCorp. Not

05:21:48.940 --> 05:21:49.480
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: immediately.

05:21:49.820 --> 05:22:05.040
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Not immediately. You had a two-year gap but you went to GenCorp and when you were in GenCorp, although no longer in PhilHealth, GenCorp was able to get contracts for PhilHealth, correct? From PhilHealth.

05:22:05.180 --> 05:22:05.420
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes.

05:22:05.860 --> 05:22:08.720
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Yes. Isn't that a conflict of interest?

05:22:09.530 --> 05:22:10.050
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: No.

05:22:10.670 --> 05:22:11.190
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Why?

05:22:13.590 --> 05:22:14.110
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Why?

05:22:14.900 --> 05:22:18.280
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: There's no conflict of interest between GenCorp and PhilHealth, ma'am.

05:22:18.460 --> 05:22:31.960
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: But you were an employee of PhilHealth and therefore could directly or indirectly influence your friends in PhilHealth to give the contract to GenCorp. I can see you're smiling. You agree?

05:22:32.400 --> 05:22:35.260
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I do not agree. That is an assumption, ma'am. Okay.

05:22:35.660 --> 05:23:29.890
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: What about securing 19 government contracts with the city of Davao? If the vice president Sara Duterte were to appear in the GIS of GenCorp as a shareholder, would GenCorp be able to get 19 government contracts from the city of Davao without it appearing that there is a conflict of interest because the city of Davao is headed? by her brother who also is the head of the procuring entity. Would that be the reason, Madam Witness, in your opinion? Would that be the reason why the

05:23:31.680 --> 05:23:39.710
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: name of the Vice President is not in the GIS so that there would be no conflict?

05:23:39.710 --> 05:23:48.630
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: of interest situation between GenCorp and the City of Davao, headed by her brother mayor

05:23:49.210 --> 05:23:52.470
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Apologies, Your Honor. Objection. It is speculative, Your Honor.

05:23:53.590 --> 05:23:59.210
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Attorney Lorna, I will have to sustain the objection. Either reform or move on to your next point, Attorney Lorna.

05:24:02.400 --> 05:24:03.600
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: We will move on, Your Honor.

05:24:05.040 --> 05:24:05.640
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you.

05:24:06.140 --> 05:24:10.940
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: The concept of beneficial ownership, Madam Witness.

05:24:11.340 --> 05:24:12.000
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, ma'am.

05:24:12.140 --> 05:24:12.740
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: You're familiar.

05:24:13.390 --> 05:24:13.990
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, ma'am.

05:24:14.090 --> 05:24:19.430
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Can you enlighten us again? What is beneficial ownership?

05:24:19.950 --> 05:24:28.010
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Beneficial owner is a natural person, ma'am, who ultimately controls or directs the decision of a certain corporation.

05:24:28.800 --> 05:24:33.240
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: So a beneficial owner is a natural person.

05:24:33.500 --> 05:24:34.400
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, ma'am.

05:24:34.740 --> 05:24:36.200
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Tao, hindi company.

05:24:36.620 --> 05:24:37.600
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Correct, ma'am.

05:24:37.620 --> 05:25:04.540
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: So when, and it is here in the forensic report. When JTC group of companies was indicated by JTC as the beneficial owner of GenCorp, and that should be, you affirm that submissions to the SEC should include beneficial ownership. You confirm that?

05:25:04.860 --> 05:25:05.380
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, ma'am.

05:25:05.500 --> 05:25:48.660
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: And in the case of GenCorp, GenCorp listed... Not a natural person. GenCorp listed in the GIS that there is a beneficial owner of certain percentage apart from JTC the person. JTC the company was listed as a beneficial owner of shares when you and I know that only Natural persons can be declared as beneficial owners.

05:25:49.440 --> 05:25:55.100
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I confirm the mistake in the Beneficial Ownership Declaration of the GIS of GenCorp.

05:25:55.400 --> 05:26:09.060
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: So there is a mistake. Thank you for that affirmation, confirmation. So there is a mistake in the submission of GenCorp declaring JTC Corp as a beneficial owner. That is a mistake.

05:26:09.400 --> 05:26:10.000
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, ma'am.

05:26:10.100 --> 05:26:11.840
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: It should be a natural person, correct?

05:26:12.380 --> 05:26:12.960
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, ma'am.

05:26:13.000 --> 05:26:18.600
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: And who, in your opinion, is that natural person?

05:26:19.930 --> 05:26:25.970
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: For now, I do not know because I do not have the records of JTC group of companies, ma'am.

05:26:26.740 --> 05:26:41.730
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: But based on this forensic report, based on latest submissions, it is the company, JTC, that's beneficial owner. But you said it is a wrong submission to the SEC.

05:26:43.170 --> 05:26:45.410
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, ma'am. I admit that it is a mistake.

05:26:45.790 --> 05:26:59.370
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Okay. Was there any, you being the in-house counsel, did you make any advice to the corporate secretary to correct that mistake?

05:26:59.940 --> 05:27:01.300
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: To amend, yes, ma'am.

05:27:01.440 --> 05:27:03.150
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: To amend? You did?

05:27:03.510 --> 05:27:04.130
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Not yet.

05:27:06.110 --> 05:27:06.890
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Not yet.

05:27:09.160 --> 05:27:19.000
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: But the GIS is as of December, end December 2025. We are already in November. 2026. You have

05:27:19.000 --> 05:27:29.620
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: not yet brought to you the attention of the company where you are sole lawyers, sole counsel to correct the statement on beneficial ownership. Not yet.

05:27:31.290 --> 05:27:35.750
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I have already advised them but the amendment has not yet been done.

05:27:36.170 --> 05:27:36.710
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: The

05:27:36.710 --> 05:27:37.230
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: beneficial

05:27:37.230 --> 05:27:39.130
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: owner, the

05:27:42.430 --> 05:27:57.710
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: beneficial owner of, based on, based on this forensic report, The beneficial owner of those shares should

05:27:59.750 --> 05:28:19.630
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: be reflected as Vice President Sara in the GIS. If we were to reconcile her admission in the SALN that she is shareholder, then the correction should be, agree or not agree with me,

05:28:20.250 --> 05:28:24.060
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: If she declared it, then in the SALN, then

05:28:24.060 --> 05:28:41.760
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: It should be declared also in the GIS because she said there's a mistake on beneficial ownership that she be declared in the GIS as the beneficial owner of those shares wrongly declared as belonging to JTC Corp. Do you agree?

05:28:42.280 --> 05:28:43.080
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: Objection, Your Honor.

05:28:43.080 --> 05:28:46.160
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Before you answer, Atty. Suzette. Yes, Atty. Justin.

05:28:46.380 --> 05:29:16.840
Atty. Justin Nicol B. Gular: With all due respect, misleading, Your Honor, I already asked this question directly during my direct examination to the witness. Whether the Vice President has any beneficial ownership, the categorical answer was no. Second, Your Honor, the witness has repeatedly insisted that the Vice President is not a stockholder of GenCorp Industries, Inc. So, there is no only no basis, but if you insist that point, that would be misleading, Your Honor, with all due respect.

05:29:16.960 --> 05:29:21.560
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Attorney Lorna, I will have to agree with Attorney Justin. It's a big leap.

05:29:21.880 --> 05:29:45.930
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: No, Your Honor, please. This is not a speculation. This is in line with her answer to an earlier question that declaring JTC Corp as the beneficial owner is wrong. It's a wrong declaration because a company cannot be a...

05:29:48.430 --> 05:29:58.330
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: A company cannot be a beneficial owner and she did say in her answer that she already told the GenCorp to rectify that mistake.

05:30:00.000 --> 05:30:00.900
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Yes,

05:30:01.160 --> 05:30:01.280
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: counsel.

05:30:01.280 --> 05:30:02.980
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: So my next question was...

05:30:02.980 --> 05:30:35.790
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: But it's a big leap, counsel, to say that JTC is owned by the Vice President or that JTC should be replaced by the name of the Vice President, especially given the fact that the court precisely did not allow the subpoenas to be issued to documents pertaining to JTC because the GIS attached to the request did not contain, of JTC, did not contain the name of the Vice President. So, what the Chair is saying is that it's a big leap.

05:30:36.090 --> 05:30:37.250
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Yes, Your Honor, it is.

05:30:37.410 --> 05:30:44.350
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: To say that JTC Corp. is the Vice President. In fact,

05:30:44.650 --> 05:30:46.110
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: No, Your Honor, if I may.

05:30:46.250 --> 05:30:47.090
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes, Attorney Larner.

05:30:47.290 --> 05:30:56.150
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: If I may, yes, Your Honor, if that were my, if that was what I was thinking, it is indeed a big leap. But that's not what I meant, Your Honor.

05:30:56.580 --> 05:31:41.600
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: It has no relation to VP owning shares in JTC. It is related to who is the beneficial owner if it is not JTC Corp. Who is the beneficial owner of that portion of shares of GenCorp. If it is not owned by JTC, you said it is wrongly. declared in the name of JTC, then if she knows, she's in-house, who then should be the beneficial owner of the shares in the GenCorp, not JTC.

05:31:42.120 --> 05:31:42.680
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: As

05:31:42.680 --> 05:31:59.060
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: in-house counsel, attorney Suzette, allow me, counsel. As in-house counsel, attorney Suzette. Tama naman po na dapat ilagay sa ngayon sa pinakalatest na rules ng SEC, hindi po ba yung totoong may-ari at hindi yung kumpanya lamang?

05:31:59.840 --> 05:32:00.700
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, Your Honor.

05:32:00.920 --> 05:32:24.900
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Sabi niyo po, tama naman yun, mali yung submission. So, if you know, sino po ang nagmamay-ari ng shares na nakapangalan sa JTC na principal shareholder ng GenCorp? If you will correct it. As you have advised to correct it, how would it be corrected, if you know?

05:32:25.260 --> 05:32:25.860
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: It

05:32:25.860 --> 05:32:35.220
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: will be corrected by looking at the records of JTC Group of Companies, Your Honor, to see kung sino yung stockholders of record nila.

05:32:35.640 --> 05:32:45.180
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So kailangan ilagay yung individual stockholders ng JTC at hindi JTC yung nakalagay doon. Yun yung correction na pinayo nyo.

05:32:45.610 --> 05:32:52.750
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, Your Honor. And not all the stockholders, pero kung sino lang po yung pasok doon sa beneficial owner.

05:32:53.510 --> 05:32:54.730
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Nang GenCorp.

05:32:55.910 --> 05:32:58.710
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Nang JTC Group of Companies.

05:32:59.630 --> 05:33:03.690
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Nang JTC Group of Companies na nagmamayari nga ng GenCorp.

05:33:04.590 --> 05:33:05.230
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes po.

05:33:05.350 --> 05:33:05.650
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Tama po?

05:33:05.850 --> 05:33:06.470
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, Your Honor.

05:33:06.950 --> 05:33:08.370
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Your Witness Attorney, Lorna.

05:33:10.280 --> 05:33:12.960
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Your Honor, please. I need to pee.

05:33:15.510 --> 05:33:16.570
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: May we have a drink?

05:33:18.140 --> 05:33:27.980
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: There would have been a better way to say it, Attorney Lorna. Chair will call for a bathroom and for those who need it, a back break.

05:33:29.640 --> 05:33:32.900
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Session will resume at around 3.30.

05:42:42.170 --> 05:42:45.870
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: You did not avail of the bathroom break, Attorney Suzette?

05:42:46.130 --> 05:42:47.090
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I did, Your Honor.

05:42:47.330 --> 05:42:51.770
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Okay. Good for you. Attorney Lorna, your witness.

05:42:53.550 --> 05:43:23.710
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Just a few more questions if you allow. Let us now go to Metro Chow. And as regards Metro Chow, the defense counsel for the respondent asks if the vice president is a shareholder, correct? To the extent that vice president is in the GIS a shareholder to the extent of 20%, correct?

05:43:26.600 --> 05:43:27.600
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Correct, ma'am.

05:43:27.740 --> 05:43:45.430
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Okay. And on question of counsel for the respondent, you were asked if she was an active shareholder. And in connection with that, you were asked, does she belong to the board of directors?

05:43:47.200 --> 05:43:48.480
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, I was asked.

05:43:48.700 --> 05:43:58.340
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Yes. And you were also asked, did she attend any meetings of the board of directors? And you answered no.

05:43:58.920 --> 05:43:59.980
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I answered no.

05:44:00.260 --> 05:44:10.970
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Okay. How many board of directors meetings are there in a year of GenCorp?

05:44:12.630 --> 05:44:14.010
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: GenCorp or Metro City?

05:44:14.010 --> 05:44:14.810
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: I'm sorry, of Metro.

05:44:16.580 --> 05:44:18.260
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I attend around two.

05:44:18.560 --> 05:44:19.360
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Around two.

05:44:20.050 --> 05:44:20.910
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, ma'am.

05:44:21.620 --> 05:44:27.220
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: You're saying that GenCorp has two board of directors meetings in a year?

05:44:28.610 --> 05:44:30.210
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: GenCorp. I'm sorry,

05:44:30.290 --> 05:44:31.110
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: I'm sorry. Metro.

05:44:32.360 --> 05:44:34.640
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I attend around two.

05:44:37.080 --> 05:44:37.760
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes.

05:44:38.520 --> 05:44:43.660
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: But Metro does not only have two meetings a year, correct?

05:44:45.520 --> 05:44:46.580
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Possible, ma'am.

05:44:46.880 --> 05:45:16.180
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Because that would be a violation, as you know, of the revised corporation code, which requires companies to have at least four meetings. In other words, Madam Witness, When you said you have not seen the vice president in any of the board of directors meetings, what you're saying is you have not seen her in the two meetings per year that you attend?

05:45:16.500 --> 05:45:17.280
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, ma'am.

05:45:17.380 --> 05:45:26.560
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Okay. You do not know if there are other meetings of the board of directors that she is there, but which meetings you don't attend, correct?

05:45:27.380 --> 05:45:28.300
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: That's possible.

05:45:28.600 --> 05:45:37.880
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: That's possible. Now, compensation committee. She is listed as a member of the compensation committee. Correct?

05:45:38.280 --> 05:45:38.900
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, ma'am.

05:45:39.100 --> 05:45:44.640
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: And yet you said the compensation committee is not a bylaw committee.

05:45:45.940 --> 05:45:47.800
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: It's not in the bylaws, ma'am, yes.

05:45:47.940 --> 05:45:55.140
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: You only created compensation committee to be compliant with bank regulations.

05:45:55.800 --> 05:45:56.700
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, ma'am.

05:45:56.900 --> 05:46:13.150
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: And in connection with that, You represented to the banks that there is a compensation committee and that the vice president is a member of the compensation committee.

05:46:14.030 --> 05:46:15.890
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Unfortunately so in the GIS.

05:46:16.090 --> 05:46:18.290
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: So that is a misrepresentation.

05:46:19.810 --> 05:46:22.890
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Not a misrepresentation but it is an error.

05:46:23.290 --> 05:46:29.630
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: It is an error. What is the difference between an error and a misrepresentation?

05:46:30.220 --> 05:46:42.420
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: It is an honest mistake, ma'am, on the accounting staff that prepared the GIS. And there is no intention to misrepresent that the Vice President is a member of the Compensation Committee.

05:46:42.920 --> 05:46:47.260
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: But she is listed as a member of the Compensation Committee.

05:46:47.540 --> 05:46:48.000
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes.

05:46:48.340 --> 05:46:55.520
Atty. Lorna Patajo-Kapunan: Correct. Now, meetings of shareholders. How many meetings per year does Metro have?

05:46:57.870 --> 05:47:00.670
