06:06:07.700 --> 06:06:11.780
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Ah, okay. Alright. Alright, number two, ma'am.

06:06:13.440 --> 06:06:19.680
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Is it return of capital or return on capital? Because there's a difference between the two.

06:06:20.670 --> 06:06:22.050
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Return of capital.

06:06:22.430 --> 06:06:38.890
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Return of capital. Kung return of capital, ma'am, bakit every year? I mean from 2022, simula po siya naging VP, hanggang last year meron pong return of capital na umabot po sa 2.1 something million, Madam Witness.

06:06:40.130 --> 06:06:57.290
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: As to bakit every year, I cannot answer po because I am not part of the accounting department. But for purposes of these proceedings, I requested for the data extraction from 2022 to 2025.

06:06:58.110 --> 06:07:02.850
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: All right. Mr. Presiding Officer, can you give me a few more? Well, I have two more questions for those witnesses.

06:07:03.090 --> 06:07:03.570
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes,

06:07:03.610 --> 06:07:03.850
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: you

06:07:03.850 --> 06:07:04.530
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: can

06:07:04.530 --> 06:07:06.970
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: wind up, Senator

06:07:06.970 --> 06:07:07.870
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Judge Raffi.

06:07:07.890 --> 06:08:03.730
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: All right. Sir, ma'am, parang coincidence ano, nung maging VP si VP Sara, biglang lumubo ang sales ng GenCorp to 300 million. Pero nung 2021, nag-list lang ito ng 28 million. Anong milagro o produkto po ang bininta nila? Na biglang lumobo sila. Na from 2022 hanggang 2024, umabot sa 1 billion ang sales nila. Pero bago siya naging VP, ang sales lamang po nila ay nasa few million lang po. At ang capital ay 1.25. Nung 2022 po, medyo 28 million lang po. 2021, 28 million lang po yung kanilang sales. Bakit bigla lumobo na po? From 2022, VP na siya hanggang wala po kayang conflict of interest noon, ma'am?

06:08:04.150 --> 06:08:32.320
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: If you can recall, GenCorp has five branches. And the acquisition of these branches is gradual. Hindi siya one time. So from 2021, may na-acquire na isa. 2022, may nadagdag until 2024. So considering na, Tumataas ang number ng, nadadagdagan ang number ng Jollibee stores, it follows na tumataas yung income, sir.

06:08:32.860 --> 06:08:52.720
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: How can, papano po siya? Last question, Mr. President and Officer. Papano kung tumataas? Pero sabi niyo noong 2023, 2.7 million lang. At 2024, 3.3 million lang ang net income ng company. Pero listed sales niyo po is 1 billion during this past 4 years or 2 years?

06:08:53.020 --> 06:09:01.780
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: With respect to that, I cannot give an answer on the income because I am not part of the operations din po.

06:09:01.920 --> 06:09:06.280
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Oh, okay. Well, that's all for me, Presiding Officer. Thank you, Madam Witness.

06:09:06.620 --> 06:09:07.100
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Thank you, Your Honor.

06:09:07.280 --> 06:09:17.910
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Senator Judge Erwin. Senator Judge Rafi Tulfo is recognized. If you're ready, sir, you may proceed. You have two minutes.

06:09:26.140 --> 06:09:30.580
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: So, Madam Witness, klaro tayo ngayon, return of, not on, capital.

06:09:30.820 --> 06:09:31.520
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Return of capital.

06:09:31.800 --> 06:09:42.980
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Okay. Kasi kanina, When asked to explain this return of capital, ang sagot niyo, I cannot verify the amounts because there are no written records for this investment, correct? You said that?

06:09:43.320 --> 06:09:43.860
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes.

06:09:44.240 --> 06:09:58.560
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Okay. Pero alam niyo naman, natatanongin namin ito sa iyo, yung mga ebidensya na meron ka para mapatunay doon sa sinasabi mong return of capital, yung binahit sa kanya, 2.1 million.

06:10:00.580 --> 06:10:01.140
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes,

06:10:01.140 --> 06:10:01.240
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Your

06:10:01.240 --> 06:10:01.420
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Honor.

06:10:02.160 --> 06:10:07.360
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: So anong patunay ka meron na talagang return of capital yun at hindi yung dividendo?

06:10:08.670 --> 06:10:14.790
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: There are no dividends declared and she is not entitled to dividends because she is not a stockholder.

06:10:15.110 --> 06:10:32.640
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: That is correct. On the other hand, explain to us bakit mo nasabi return of capital yun? At siyempre kung return of capital yun dapat may input. Meron siyang inilagay na pera doon sa kumpanya na para maibalik sa kanya yung capital niya.

06:10:33.040 --> 06:10:38.260
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: You are correct, Your Honor. May nailagay nga po siyang pera sa Davao Bounty, which did not push through.

06:10:38.460 --> 06:10:39.460
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: 46,000.

06:10:40.320 --> 06:10:49.180
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Ang Articles of Incorporation, 46,000. I do not know if there are other investments kasi yung 46,000 is the creation of a corporation.

06:10:49.260 --> 06:10:53.660
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Correct. At hindi na tuloy. So from 46,000, nakatanggap siya ng 2.1 million pabalik

06:10:53.660 --> 06:10:54.700
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: sa kapitan niyo.

06:10:54.740 --> 06:10:55.960
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: So paano nangyari yun?

06:11:00.480 --> 06:11:01.720
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Paano nangyari na?

06:11:02.420 --> 06:11:11.740
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: From 46,000, ininvest niya doon sa Davao Bounty at ibinalik sa kanya sa return of capital niya, 2.1 million. Paano nangyari yun? Do the math. Do the math.

06:11:11.980 --> 06:11:15.760
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: The 46,000 is the creation of the corporation.

06:11:16.400 --> 06:11:16.820
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Okay.

06:11:16.900 --> 06:11:27.080
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: So, I do not know if there were other investments made na hindi nakareflect sa articles of incorporation.

06:11:27.720 --> 06:11:42.480
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: At alam mo, pag-uusapan natin yan ngayon, bakit hindi ka mag-gumawa ng research? 15 years ka abogado at accountant ka pa at that. So you should have at least done some research and then at the same time did some asking. Why didn't you do that?

06:11:42.620 --> 06:11:56.200
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yun nga po ang ginawa ko and I did not find any verifiable document. So I cannot produce paper out of thin air. So apologies if I cannot give a figure.

06:11:57.060 --> 06:11:58.020
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Then you're

06:11:58.020 --> 06:12:06.440
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: not a credible witness in that way, in this case. Kasi wala kang nasasabi sa amin eh. Puro I do not know.

06:12:06.820 --> 06:12:11.660
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I leave that to the judgment of the Honorable Senator-Judges, Your Honor.

06:12:11.900 --> 06:12:14.880
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Yes, for me. Because it's very simple.

06:12:16.390 --> 06:12:36.420
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Just do the math. Sinabi kanina, 46,000, nag-invest siya doon sa Davao Bounty na hindi natuloy na maging franchise pag-aari ng Gian Court later on. Ibinabalik sa kanya. Ay 41 million as a return of her investment. Hindi mo ma-explain. Nasaan yung mga kontrata? Nasaan yung mga cancelled checks? Do you have a copy of the cancelled checks?

06:12:37.330 --> 06:12:40.610
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: As stated earlier, I do not have a copy of the cancelled checks.

06:12:41.330 --> 06:12:52.250
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Alam mo na maging testigo ka dito tungkol dito sa paksang ito. Hindi ka man lang humingi ng kopya ng mga dokumento tulad ng cancelled checks, tulad nitong contracts, etc.

06:12:53.070 --> 06:12:55.130
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: If I may, Your Honor, I believe

06:12:57.860 --> 06:13:15.780
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Witnesses from the bank would also be presented so the body can verify if the amounts that I submitted to this honorable court matches with the bank records.

06:13:16.400 --> 06:13:25.490
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: No, kasi yung canceled checks, ibinabalik doon sa nag-issue, which happens to be GenCorp, diba? Nag-issue lang tseke kay VP Sara.

06:13:25.810 --> 06:13:26.830
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: You are correct, Your Honor.

06:13:26.970 --> 06:13:31.980
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Then, why didn't you ask GenCorp? Copy of the canceled check. Eh total, ikaw in-house counsel.

06:13:32.260 --> 06:13:35.720
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I did not anymore ask for the copy.

06:13:35.720 --> 06:13:36.000
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Why not?

06:13:36.020 --> 06:13:36.560
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Alam mo naman,

06:13:36.560 --> 06:13:37.520
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: matitisigo ka tungkol

06:13:37.520 --> 06:13:37.760
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: dito.

06:13:38.020 --> 06:13:46.920
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: The fastest way that I can provide the information that these honorable senator judges might need is through data extraction.

06:13:48.150 --> 06:14:32.290
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Madam witness, meron akong mga researcher dyan na nag-aaral sa law school, second year college. Para sa akin, this is my own opinion. Mas magaling pa mag-research sa iyo or nagmaang-maangan ka lang. I'm sorry ha kasi ilang araw na nag-present ng testigo tong defense na parang nalilito kami eh. It's either may tinatago or ayaw sabihin kung ano talaga yung totoo or kulang kayo sa kaalaman. I don't know which is which. But really, you know na mag-tetestigo ka tungkol sa GenCorp. And you should have came here prepared. E pumunta ka rito, maraming mga butas sa iyo na hindi mo masagot-sagot, mga simpleng katanungan.

06:14:33.980 --> 06:14:37.180
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Tulad nitong, last na lamang po, Mr. Presiding Officer.

06:14:37.420 --> 06:14:38.440
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes, you may wind up, sir.

06:14:40.090 --> 06:14:40.530
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Okay.

06:14:43.020 --> 06:14:43.460
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: When

06:14:48.550 --> 06:14:54.970
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: you say there are no written records, did you mean wala talaga? Tama? Wala?

06:14:55.070 --> 06:14:55.470
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, Your Honor.

06:14:55.770 --> 06:14:59.990
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: So, nakadrawing lang sa hangin lahat ng transaksyon ng Jollibee Times Square, kung gano'n?

06:15:01.660 --> 06:15:06.300
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Not Jollibee Times Square, Your Honor. No written records with respect to Davao Bounty.

06:15:06.830 --> 06:15:22.060
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: No written records. So, ibig sabihin, wala kang ginawa talagang pag-hahalughog or pag-reresearch o pag-tatatanong. Dahil babalik ko sa sinabi kanina, alam niyo po na kayo magtitisigot tungkol sa Gen Corp.

06:15:23.880 --> 06:16:13.050
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Unexplainable wealth ang pinag-uusapan natin dito. And you're here to explain to us how did it happen and how it happened. And nalilito ka eh. Pati kami nalilito na rin sa mga nakakalito mong kasagutan. Lastly, very simple. Hindi mo mai-account sa amin yung 2.1 million na ibinalay ka sa return of capital from 46,000 na in-invest niya sa Davao Bounty. At yung explanation mo very flimsy at kahit na siguro elementary, mahirapan ma-connect eh. Kasi you have to have documents. Diba? You have to have contracts para mapatunayan na yung 46,000 ay naging 2.1 million, papaano?

06:16:14.800 --> 06:16:19.950
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Doon pala nga sa 46,000, do you have a document tungkol sa 46,000 na?

06:16:20.010 --> 06:16:21.910
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, Your Honor, the Articles of Incorporation.

06:16:21.950 --> 06:16:31.750
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: You have that, right. Okay. Doon sa contract na para naging 2.1 million yung 46,000, do you have a document?

06:16:32.220 --> 06:16:36.080
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I am not aware if any such contract exists. I did not see anyone.

06:16:36.200 --> 06:16:36.220
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Exactly.

06:16:36.320 --> 06:16:55.500
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Precisely. Correct. Then you should have at least inquired. Being the house counsel, being the in-house counsel, you should have asked your colleagues o kung sino ba mga opisyal doon sa gem court, nasaan na ang kontrata para dito kasi iniimbitahan ako maging witness. Come on.

06:16:56.280 --> 06:16:57.360
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I did, Your Honor.

06:16:57.580 --> 06:16:57.900
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: You

06:16:57.900 --> 06:16:59.320
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: did. And then what did they do?

06:17:00.550 --> 06:17:01.270
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: And then?

06:17:02.090 --> 06:17:03.470
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: There are no contracts.

06:17:03.890 --> 06:17:05.130
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: So walang kontrata.

06:17:05.990 --> 06:17:07.650
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I did not see any contract.

06:17:08.920 --> 06:17:12.340
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: So ibig sabihin, yung usapang hangin lang ito.

06:17:13.150 --> 06:17:13.670
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Or

06:17:13.670 --> 06:17:14.650
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: under the table.

06:17:15.270 --> 06:17:17.590
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I will not speculate on that.

06:17:17.870 --> 06:17:46.550
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: No, kasi sabi mo walang kontrata eh. When in fact, we're talking about serious business to ah. Hindi naman ito yung mga sari-sari store. Malaking kumpanya ito, korporasyon ito. You ask and then they said there is no contract. Then you should ask them, bakit walang contract? Kasi kung ako, I will push on. Okay, there's no contract being in-house counsel. Teka muna, bakit wala pong contract? Eh, tatanungin sa akin pagdating ko sa impeachment court, they will ask me that. What would I tell them?

06:17:48.280 --> 06:17:52.700
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Dito kayo naipit. And you're a lawyer for 15 years, you said.

06:17:55.660 --> 06:18:05.620
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Like I said, mga researcher dito sa Senate, siguro, mas kina nag-aaral pa sa law school, baka pinagtatawan ka. That's just my opinion. Thank you. Mr. Presiding Officer.

06:18:07.590 --> 06:18:12.010
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Senator Judge Pangilinan is recognized. You have two minutes, sir. You may proceed when you're ready.

06:18:14.200 --> 06:18:18.600
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer. Magandang hapon, Attorney.

06:18:19.240 --> 06:18:20.460
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Good afternoon, Your Honor.

06:18:21.440 --> 06:18:26.380
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Yes. I will just follow up on the questions raised earlier by Senator Rafi.

06:18:28.040 --> 06:18:47.270
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: So, kasi nung ikaw ay nasa direct examination, maliwanag sa'yo. Walang participation whatsoever si Vice President Sara Duterte sa GenCorp management. Walang participation whatsoever. Zero participation. Tama po ba?

06:18:47.900 --> 06:18:49.240
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: That is correct, Your Honor.

06:18:49.400 --> 06:18:55.390
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Yes. No stock holdings. She has no position. Tama po ba?

06:18:55.730 --> 06:18:56.830
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: That is correct, Your Honor.

06:18:56.850 --> 06:18:57.030
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: And

06:18:57.030 --> 06:19:16.050
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: you said no participation whatsoever. So, and then, when we started... When the presiding officer, and I think again in direct examination, you mentioned that she actually had a loose investment. She was a loose investor. Tama?

06:19:16.730 --> 06:19:18.650
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: There is a loose investment, Your Honor, yes.

06:19:18.710 --> 06:19:22.950
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Okay. So, and she was receiving benefits from that loose investment?

06:19:23.710 --> 06:19:25.110
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: There were disbursements, yes.

06:19:25.150 --> 06:19:35.590
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: So, okay. So, zero? No participation whatsoever? Or? Merong konting participation dun sa kaunti mong nalalamang participation.

06:19:37.220 --> 06:19:44.060
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: As far as I am aware, Your Honor, she has no participation in the management and in the operations of the business.

06:19:44.420 --> 06:20:17.300
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: You were also asked about no role whatsoever. But receiving benefits, you are a recipient. Then you have a role. Ikaw ay tumatanggap ng benepisyo. Beneficiary ka nung So, it's not correct to say that there is no participation or no role whatsoever. You participated as a beneficiary. Are you saying, therefore, that it's not exactly accurate that she had no role whatsoever?

06:20:18.750 --> 06:20:23.810
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: The way I understand the word participate in business is

06:20:23.810 --> 06:20:31.150
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: a beneficiary is somebody who benefits from monies. Isn't that being a participant?

06:20:31.430 --> 06:20:34.210
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: One who benefits from money is a recipient, yes.

06:20:34.230 --> 06:20:47.930
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Exactly. So it's incorrect. Let's be clear here. You said you were so categorical, you were so clear, na no participation whatsoever. And now it's turning out, meron pala. Tama. Meron as a recipient.

06:20:48.610 --> 06:20:49.590
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: As a recipient,

06:20:49.650 --> 06:20:49.670
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: yes.

06:20:50.110 --> 06:20:50.570
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Okay.

06:20:50.570 --> 06:21:19.590
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Now, my next question is, nung tinanong ka about being a recipient, at tinanong ka ng presiding officer, ano ba itong arrangement na ito? Sabi mo, it's a loose agreement, loose investment. You were the one who used the term. And then, tinanong ka ni Senator Bam, you're familiar with what was received in 2022, 2023, 2024, tama? But you're not familiar with 2026.

06:21:20.070 --> 06:21:20.770
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: That is correct.

06:21:21.190 --> 06:21:21.650
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Why not?

06:21:21.850 --> 06:21:25.410
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I did not ask for the 2026 if there was any.

06:21:25.630 --> 06:21:25.990
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Why not?

06:21:26.700 --> 06:21:29.660
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Because the subpoena is 2022 to 2025.

06:21:30.380 --> 06:21:43.990
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Yes, but if these questions were raised, you would have been able to explore further what exactly is going on. I raised that question because is it possible that there are other...

06:21:44.310 --> 06:21:45.610
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: It is possible.

06:21:46.050 --> 06:21:57.880
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: And you don't know that. So, di ba? Kasi limang kumpanya yun eh. So, posible bang merong ibang... Binibigyan ang accounting na hindi mo alam dahil hindi mo natanong.

06:21:59.460 --> 06:22:02.340
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: May I clarify on the limang kumpanya, your honor?

06:22:03.060 --> 06:22:06.180
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Well, okay, go ahead, please. Branches, the branches.

06:22:06.480 --> 06:22:06.720
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Limang

06:22:06.720 --> 06:22:07.660
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: branches, your honor, yes.

06:22:07.840 --> 06:22:19.600
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Yes, in other words, these other five branches can be providing additional compensation, income, loose return on investment, but you wouldn't know.

06:22:21.240 --> 06:22:32.060
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: The data extracted from 2022 to 2025 is everything that GenCorp has disbursed and it all came from Times Square branch only.

06:22:33.270 --> 06:22:34.770
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: But there are four branches.

06:22:35.230 --> 06:22:49.530
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: That is why the data extracted is for the whole GenCorp. So meaning the whole five branches and yung lumabas na data na sinubmit ko dito.

06:22:51.280 --> 06:22:52.000
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Galing

06:22:52.000 --> 06:22:54.620
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: lang lahat sa Times Square branch.

06:22:54.760 --> 06:23:17.760
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: I'll go through my second round. Forgive me, Attorney, but earlier you were so clear and categorical that there was no participation whatsoever. And now, meron pala as a loose investor. Kasi loose investment. So investor siya. Loose lang nga. So medyo, I'd like to know, what else don't you know? Or what else are you

06:23:19.660 --> 06:23:26.220
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Not really categorical about. I'm just raising these questions. I have no answer. I'm just raising these questions at this time.

06:23:26.920 --> 06:23:27.540
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Thank you.

06:23:27.960 --> 06:23:35.040
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Senator Judge Kiko. Senator Judge Sotto is recognized. The former Senate President. You have two minutes, sir. You may proceed when you're ready.

06:23:39.240 --> 06:23:46.620
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Mr. Presiding Officer, thank you, kind sir. Atty. Punay, you know.

06:23:47.640 --> 06:23:48.700
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Good afternoon, Your Honor.

06:23:48.700 --> 06:23:50.320
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Good afternoon, witness. Yes, good afternoon.

06:23:52.050 --> 06:23:55.130
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: You are familiar, of course, with corporation law.

06:23:55.840 --> 06:23:56.660
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, Your Honor.

06:23:56.920 --> 06:24:04.860
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Yeah, okay. Before that, what does GenCorp stand for? Ano yung G-E-N?

06:24:06.110 --> 06:24:08.350
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Nothing, Your Honor. It's just GenCorp.

06:24:09.560 --> 06:24:10.840
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Doesn't stand for anything?

06:24:13.650 --> 06:24:14.990
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: So yung GEN, wala?

06:24:15.110 --> 06:24:16.530
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Wala. If

06:24:16.530 --> 06:24:21.370
