Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, Your Honor.

07:39:57.730 --> 07:39:59.850
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: You're right. Is that right?

07:40:00.240 --> 07:40:03.960
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: If it was intentionally and deliberately done, Your Honor.

07:40:03.960 --> 07:40:25.610
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Yes, okay. Just for the record. Now, with respect to, is it possible that the reason why she placed it in her SALN is because precisely she's been receiving this return in investments? Would that be possible? In the realm of the possible?

07:40:27.050 --> 07:40:27.670
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Possible.

07:40:28.050 --> 07:40:56.050
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Okay. Except that, It should have been reflected in her SALN and also on 2022 and 2023. Because based on your record or your information, the return on investments were given or return on capital were received 2022, 2023, 2024, and 2025.

07:40:56.510 --> 07:40:57.090
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, Your Honor.

07:40:57.350 --> 07:41:00.780
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: So medyo may gap pa doon. Okay.

07:41:04.220 --> 07:41:21.840
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: So, on the matter of going back to the loose investment, when did you find out about the loose investments being turned over to the Vice President?

07:41:22.160 --> 07:41:26.380
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: When I conducted the study on the history of the corporations.

07:41:26.860 --> 07:41:27.900
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: So, a long time ago?

07:41:28.440 --> 07:41:34.750
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: No. When the impeachment... Impeachment time na.

07:41:35.090 --> 07:41:36.250
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: So about July?

07:41:37.070 --> 07:41:38.530
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Probably, probably July.

07:41:38.550 --> 07:41:53.150
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Okay, so in other words, you had enough time to ask for the documents, supporting documents, etc. But again, from July up until today, you were unable to secure the documentation.

07:41:54.300 --> 07:41:58.220
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I requested for the data extraction last week.

07:41:58.640 --> 07:42:04.520
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Yes. How did you find out through the documents?

07:42:06.960 --> 07:42:09.380
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Nakita lang ninyo na may tinatanggap pala siya?

07:42:09.850 --> 07:42:11.230
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I requested po.

07:42:11.670 --> 07:42:13.050
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: You requested accounting?

07:42:13.570 --> 07:42:14.090
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes.

07:42:14.450 --> 07:42:16.070
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Okay, and then they gave it to you?

07:42:16.270 --> 07:42:16.750
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes.

07:42:16.930 --> 07:42:21.070
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: But no supporting documents, just a list of the monies received?

07:42:21.530 --> 07:42:22.170
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes.

07:42:22.510 --> 07:42:53.790
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Okay, so that's where the trouble is. And I hope you understand. You have no supporting documents. For now. For now. That's why we're requesting it. And that's why it's difficult just for the figures being presented to us. We believe we need supporting documents to be able to better understand this matter of return of capital. So we'd like to thank Senator

07:42:57.150 --> 07:43:07.090
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Erwin for requesting that so that we can better understand. Kasi mahirap naman na we will just take your word for it without the necessary supporting documents. I hope you understand.

07:43:07.330 --> 07:43:07.910
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, Your Honor.

07:43:08.290 --> 07:43:19.980
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: And one last, just to yung sa external auditor, you saw the qualified opinion, you said that, you read it. I

07:43:19.980 --> 07:43:20.840
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: read it, Your Honor.

07:43:20.940 --> 07:43:40.680
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Could you, so sinabi doon, We are not able to verify the cash account and observe physical counting of inventories due to certain limitations imposed by the management. What are these limitations imposed by management? Would you know?

07:43:41.140 --> 07:43:42.160
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: No, Your Honor.

07:43:42.740 --> 07:43:43.660
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Did you ask?

07:43:44.220 --> 07:43:44.820
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: No.

07:43:45.280 --> 07:43:46.060
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Why not?

07:43:46.620 --> 07:43:48.060
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I did not ask.

07:43:48.280 --> 07:43:57.220
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Why not? Because you're supposed to provide them legal advice on legal inquiries.

07:43:58.820 --> 07:44:08.480
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: You don't want to have a qualified opinion from your external auditors if you're a company serious about your operations, right?

07:44:09.760 --> 07:44:10.360
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes.

07:44:10.440 --> 07:44:21.240
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: So, is it not your duty to at least inquire as to why, what were the limitations, and provide the right advice as a lawyer, as their in-house general counsel?

07:44:22.340 --> 07:44:23.240
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I did not.

07:44:24.280 --> 07:44:42.790
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Okay. So, and you said earlier that you were supposed to, you know, your role is to address legal inquiries, etc. But in this case, you did not do that. And one last question. Sabi mo kanina na you're not aware whether the employees were contractual or regular?

07:44:44.530 --> 07:44:45.230
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I am

07:44:45.230 --> 07:44:49.430
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: not aware kung ilan po yung regular or contractual.

07:44:49.490 --> 07:44:51.930
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: So, ilan ang empleyado? Hindi lang dalawa.

07:44:52.390 --> 07:44:57.010
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Hindi ko rin po alam kung ano yung exact number ng empleyado namin.

07:44:57.850 --> 07:45:03.570
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: And your role is also on employee discipline as counsel, right?

07:45:03.970 --> 07:45:04.630
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes po.

07:45:05.110 --> 07:45:11.660
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: So you're not, you don't know how many employees there are? You don't know whether they are contractual or regular?

07:45:12.080 --> 07:45:14.180
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I do not know the exact numbers po.

07:45:14.680 --> 07:45:17.020
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: But you're in charge of employee discipline?

07:45:17.570 --> 07:45:27.270
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I am in charge of employee discipline in the manner that I do investigations kung may mga, for example, may pilferage. Ganun po.

07:45:29.200 --> 07:45:31.380
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Okay. No further questions.

07:45:31.980 --> 07:45:37.140
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Senator Judge Riza. You may proceed, ma'am. You have two minutes when you're ready.

07:45:43.190 --> 07:46:09.700
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Salamat, Mr. Presiding Officer. Attorney Suzette, sabi niyo kanina, direktor pa rin si VP Duterte ng Metro City Chow Corporation noong 2022 hanggang 2025. Nung 2022, nung naging VP na siya, nag-attempt ba siyang mag-recuse or umalis bilang corporate director?

07:46:10.320 --> 07:46:12.960
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I am not aware if there is such an attempt.

07:46:16.220 --> 07:46:24.020
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Pero sumototal, hindi siya umalis, andun pa rin siya hanggang 2025 at least. Stockholder

07:46:24.020 --> 07:46:24.780
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: pa rin po siya.

07:46:26.790 --> 07:46:33.570
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Yung pagiging corporate director. Corporate director pa rin siya. Yes. Hanggang last year at least. Okay po.

07:46:33.730 --> 07:46:34.090
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, Your Honor.

07:46:34.390 --> 07:46:39.010
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: And then, tungkol naman sa mga kontrata sa Davao LGU.

07:46:40.750 --> 07:46:50.170
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Alam po ba ninyo na si VP Duterte ay naging business partner ni Jaime T. Cruz sa mga kumpanyang pinag-uusapan natin?

07:46:52.410 --> 07:46:55.730
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: They are both stockholders in Metro City Chow.

07:46:56.090 --> 07:47:47.720
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Yes, so may business relationship sila as stockholders. Specifically sa Metro City Chow Foods nga po, alimbawa, si VP Sara ay may 20% ng shares, habang si Jaime T. Cruz ay may halos 80%. Yun naman pong kapatid ni VP na si Mayor Sebastian Duterte, sa Grand King's Food at Grand MD Business Development, mayroon siyang tig 5% ng shares ng dalawang kumpanyang iyon. Sa SPMC Chow Foods, 15%. At sa Times Square Chow Foods, 20%. At may shares din siya sa Chinese Gen B Food Corporation. Aware po ba kayo dito?

07:47:50.050 --> 07:47:58.810
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I'm not aware of the stock holdings of Baste and all those other corporations that you have mentioned, Your Honor.

07:47:59.950 --> 07:48:05.030
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Pero aware kayo na mayroon siyang stock holdings doon kahit di niyo alam yung percentages?

07:48:05.590 --> 07:48:07.690
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: From your statement.

07:48:08.090 --> 07:48:14.230
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: From my statement. Hindi niyo po alam ito bago ko itinanong sa inyong ngayong hapon?

07:48:14.470 --> 07:48:15.610
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: No, Your Honor. I'm sorry.

07:48:18.320 --> 07:48:30.200
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Kino-confirm niyo po ba na ang GenCorp ay inawardan ng labing siyam na kontrata ng administrasyon ni Mayor Sebastian Duterte, ang kapatid ni VP Duterte?

07:48:30.540 --> 07:48:30.900
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes,

07:48:30.900 --> 07:48:31.280
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Your Honor.

07:48:33.760 --> 07:48:41.300
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Itong parehong GenCorp na may declared interest, winding up with one last question, Mr. Presiding Officer.

07:48:41.300 --> 07:48:41.680
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes, please.

07:48:42.020 --> 07:49:09.190
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Salamat po. Yung same-GenCorp na may declared interest ang vicepresidente na kapatid ni Mayor Duterte at yung same-GenCorp na may controlling interest yung JTC group of companies na yung may-ari ay si Jaime T. Cruz na documented close business associate ni Mayor Duterte, ni Mayor Sebastian Duterte.

07:49:09.510 --> 07:49:10.650
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, Your Honor.

07:49:11.630 --> 07:49:36.290
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: So, huling tanong po para sa akin ngayong hapon para sa inyo. Bilang corporate counsel, kung may posibleng conflict of interest sa pagitan ng inyong kumpanya at isang government official na may personal interest or family business connections sa inyong shareholders,

07:49:37.980 --> 07:49:41.500
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Tungkulin po ba ninyong i-flag ito sa management ninyo?

07:49:41.680 --> 07:49:42.380
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, Your Honor.

07:49:42.680 --> 07:50:04.660
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Yes, ma'am. So, at hindi po ba na tungkulin nyo nga ito para masiguro na sumusunod ang inyong kumpanya sa batas, masiguro na maiwasan yung mga questionable transaction, masiguro na maprotektahan ang kumpanya laban sa posibleng legal liability?

07:50:05.200 --> 07:50:06.160
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, Your Honor.

07:50:06.360 --> 07:50:07.040
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Yes, ma'am.

07:50:07.740 --> 07:50:14.980
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Kasi nga, kung magkakasuhan man, kayo din po ang sasagot, kayo din po ang haharap po, di po ba?

07:50:15.620 --> 07:50:16.540
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: There's a possibility.

07:50:17.120 --> 07:50:18.060
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: There's a possibility.

07:50:18.960 --> 07:50:19.380
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Yes,

07:50:19.380 --> 07:50:19.680
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: ma'am.

07:50:20.820 --> 07:50:26.380
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: So, muli, Atty. Suzette, dagang salamat. Salamat po, Mr. Presiding Officer.

07:50:26.780 --> 07:50:27.160
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank

07:50:27.160 --> 07:50:42.420
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: you, Senator Judge Riza. Just a few questions, Mr. Presiding Officer, Atty. Suzette, bear with us. I assure you, we will let you go before 6 and we will be adjourned before 6. Unang tanong po, saan po ang main office address ng GenCorp?

07:50:43.160 --> 07:50:51.080
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: GenCorp is 3rd floor, PVL building, Bolton, Corner, Rizal Street. Bolton Street.

07:50:51.520 --> 07:50:55.800
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So may Jollibee branch din po sa parehong building kung saan may opisina ang GenCorp.

07:50:56.200 --> 07:50:57.640
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: That is correct, Your Honor.

07:50:57.880 --> 07:51:18.240
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So, dun sa bidding documents ng GenCorp, yung sinasabi ni Senate President kaninang 19 contracts. na nakalagay GenCorp Bolton. Ang ibig sabihin po nun, GenCorp na may address sa Bolton at hindi automatic ang nangangahulugang Jollibee Bolton yung nanalo sa bidding.

07:51:20.450 --> 07:51:21.150
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kanina

07:51:21.150 --> 07:51:43.730
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: po kasi nabanggit niyo nung tinatanong kayo ng Atty. Justin na yung mga kontrata ay galing sa apat na branches maliban sa Times Square. Pero nung pinasuri ko po kasi yung mga bidding documents, hindi naman po nakalagay yung particular na Jollibee branch na binigyan ng award. So ano po ang basihan ninyo doon?

07:51:43.970 --> 07:51:48.770
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Ang binibigyan po ng award is the corporation kasi siya po yung may...

07:51:48.770 --> 07:51:49.150
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Exactly.

07:51:49.450 --> 07:52:06.380
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Tinanong po kayo kanina kung meron po ba na nakuha ang kontrata ang Jollibee sa Times Square. Kung tama pagkakaalala ko, sabi niyo po wala. Pero ang nananalo po sa bidding, GenCorp. Hindi naman po yung Jollibee branch na pag-aari ng GenCorp. Tama po ba?

07:52:07.250 --> 07:52:07.970
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Correct, Your Honor.

07:52:08.150 --> 07:52:15.650
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Hindi naman po nagbibid yung branch ng Jollibee na pag-aari ng GenCorp. Ang nagbibid po ay GenCorp. Tama po.

07:52:15.710 --> 07:52:16.810
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: GenCorp ang nagbibid.

07:52:16.830 --> 07:52:22.610
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kung sino man po magsusupply dun sa limang branch, eh problema na po ng GenCorp. Yan yung nanalong bidder.

07:52:23.290 --> 07:52:24.030
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, Your Honor.

07:52:24.210 --> 07:52:37.520
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Would that be correct? Okay. Next point, Atty. Suzette. Ano po ang relasyon ni Jaime kay Richie? Parehong apelido, Cruz.

07:52:38.340 --> 07:52:38.940
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Mag-asawa.

07:52:39.000 --> 07:52:39.480
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Mag-asawa.

07:52:39.480 --> 07:52:49.820
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: These are interlocking directors of the various companies mentioned. Whether it's Davao Bounty, Great Jolly, Great Jolly Times, Times Square B, GenCorp, diba? So, ganyan. Ano pong relasyon nila?

07:52:50.000 --> 07:52:51.300
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Spouses, Your Honor.

07:52:51.560 --> 07:52:55.470
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Asawa po ni Jaime si Richie. Si Kimberly po.

07:52:56.200 --> 07:52:56.920
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Anak po.

07:52:57.750 --> 07:53:00.410
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Si Nathan Zachary po.

07:53:00.990 --> 07:53:01.870
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Anak din po.

07:53:02.270 --> 07:53:03.630
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Si Girly po.

07:53:04.700 --> 07:53:06.320
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: No relation po.

07:53:07.120 --> 07:53:14.580
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So Dela Cruz na siya, yung Cruz niya, walang relation sa Cruz nila. So yung tatlo lang po yung magkakamag-anak?

07:53:15.260 --> 07:53:15.840
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Apat.

07:53:16.140 --> 07:53:23.400
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Apat po, magkakamag-anak. So mag-asawa at nanay-tatay? Magkapatid?

07:53:23.700 --> 07:53:24.660
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, Your Honor.

07:53:26.200 --> 07:53:36.980
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Sabi niyo po, binabayaran si VP Sara, nung accountant, sa halagang 2 million ng 22 to 25 dahil dun sa interest niya sa Davao Bounty. Tama po ba?

07:53:37.200 --> 07:53:38.120
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, Your Honor.

07:53:38.580 --> 07:53:52.570
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Nilagay po ng Vice President sa kanyang SALN noong 2007 na incorporator stockholder siya ng Davao Bounty. Noong 2013, nilagay na po niya na siya ay stockholder ng

07:53:57.600 --> 07:54:18.540
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: ng Great Jolly Times, sorry, noong 2015. Sabi po dito, Great Jolly Times Food slash Times Square B Foods Corporation. Katulad lang po ng ginawa niya sa GenCorp. Nilagay din po niyang stockholder siya. Pero, sa pagkakaalam niyo, stockholder po ba siya ng dalawang kumpanyang to?

07:54:19.120 --> 07:54:22.700
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I will base it only on the articles of incorporation, Your Honor.

07:54:22.720 --> 07:54:23.060
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Exactly.

07:54:23.200 --> 07:54:24.920
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Based on that, is she a stockholder?

07:54:25.040 --> 07:54:25.920
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: She's not, right? She's

07:54:25.920 --> 07:54:26.780
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: not, Your Honor.

07:54:27.120 --> 07:54:35.180
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: She's not a stockholder of Great Jolly Times Food Corporation and she's not a stockholder of Times Square B Foods Corporation, correct?

07:54:35.820 --> 07:54:36.760
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Correct, Your Honor.

07:54:37.810 --> 07:54:41.190
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Neither is she a stockholder of GenCorp Corporation.

07:54:43.320 --> 07:54:44.080
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, Your Honor.

07:54:44.280 --> 07:55:12.130
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: And yet, she placed all of these companies in her SALN as incorporator stockholder. Now, will it be reasonable for us to also assume that she was receiving something from these defunct corporations as well? Namely, Great Jolly Times Food Corporation and Times Square Food Corporation. Would you be aware of any such amounts received by the Vice President from these companies prior to GenCorp?

07:55:12.580 --> 07:55:17.920
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I am not aware if there were disbursements from those companies, Your Honor.

07:55:18.100 --> 07:55:22.480
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Now, I'm still on this subject matter, ma'am. Tinayo yung Jollibee sa Times Square ng 2007, correct?

07:55:23.210 --> 07:55:23.990
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, Your Honor.

07:55:24.110 --> 07:55:26.990
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Never napunta sa Davao Bounty yung prangkisa?

07:55:27.370 --> 07:55:28.770
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: That is correct, Your Honor.

07:55:29.030 --> 07:55:39.190
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Ano po ang kailangan bayaran ng Great Jolly Times sa Davao Bounty kung hindi naman sa kanya napunta yung prangkisa? Sa kanya po ba yung lease nung lugar?

07:55:40.000 --> 07:55:40.920
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: No, Your Honor.

07:55:41.450 --> 07:55:42.970
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Hindi rin sa kanya yung prangkisa.

07:55:44.000 --> 07:55:44.560
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Hindi

07:55:44.560 --> 07:56:12.910
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: rin bahagi si VP Sara ng Great Jolly Times bagaman nilagay niya sa SALN niya. So ano po yung kailangang pagbayaran at ano po yung investment na pinasa-pasa o minana-mana ng mga kumpanya na hindi nasama ang pangalan ng VP dun sa mga kumpanya ngayon, namely Great Jolly Times, Times Square, and GenCorp later on. What exactly is the consideration for these monies being given to her?

07:56:14.090 --> 07:56:17.290
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: For the consideration, Your Honor, I do not know.

07:56:18.530 --> 07:56:19.090
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Ma

07:56:19.090 --> 07:56:36.680
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: 'am, you are very specific. You mentioned it is for the Davao bounty. Yes. So what is the interest of Davao bounty in all of this? When they do not own the lease, they do not own the franchise, so what's the whole point in compensating Davao bounty?

07:56:37.020 --> 07:56:50.190
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: To my understanding, Your Honor, is the investment in the form of contributions she may have made before the operations of Great Jolly Times.

07:56:50.690 --> 07:56:51.070
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: I

07:56:51.070 --> 07:57:01.000
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: agree, but ibang kompanya yun eh. Hindi naman siya bahagi ng Great Jolly Times, ma'am eh. Again, nilagay niya na sa Stockholder Incorporated pero hindi siya bahagi nun ayon sa GIS.

07:57:01.480 --> 07:57:01.820
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes.

07:57:01.960 --> 07:57:17.600
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So ano po yung binili, binayaran ng Great Jolly Times? Ano po yung binili, binayaran kung meron man ng Times Square? Ano po yung binabayaran hanggang noong 2025 at least ng GenCorp? Didn't it raise a big question mark on your part?

07:57:18.210 --> 07:57:19.490
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: It did, Your Honor.

07:57:20.850 --> 07:57:27.910
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So, sabi mo hindi sa kanya yung prangkisa, hindi sa kanya yung lease. So, what is it for, ma'am?

07:57:28.150 --> 07:57:38.150
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: I cannot pinpoint for certain kung ano. So, based sa inquiry and

07:57:39.690 --> 07:57:40.250
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Those

07:57:40.250 --> 07:57:45.530
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: were the expenses before nag-operate ang Jollibee.

07:57:45.730 --> 07:58:14.600
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: But this was way back in 2007, ma'am. And the only evidence you've given us is amounts given in 2022 to 2025. Again, I'm assuming na malamang mula noong 2007 pa din to. This is quite a serious allegation, ma'am, from a different perspective. The vice president during different times in her career was a public officer. So why would she be receiving monies from a private corporation that she has no interest in?

07:58:16.480 --> 07:59:11.630
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Hindi po ba? Yung period na in question, dala niyo po yung sa accountant, yung 2022 to 2025, you just testified under oath that she was receiving monies from a private corporation in relation to a company she owned way back in 2007. that has no ownership over a franchise, no leasehold rights over the property where the Jollibee is located, and yet she is receiving money from a private corporation. I think it behooves on your part, especially given that you are a witness for the defense, to kindly explain via the submission of documents requested by Senator Judge Erwin and the Presiding Officer What these monies are for? In order to clear the air and to prove that these are not illegal or in any way violative of any laws. Do you agree, ma'am?

07:59:11.890 --> 07:59:12.570
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, your honor.

07:59:13.630 --> 07:59:17.430
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you. So we will still issue the subpoena, ma'am? You need it?

07:59:17.850 --> 07:59:18.490
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Yes, your honor.

07:59:23.050 --> 07:59:28.910
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: We will do so, ma'am. And we will just send it to you via... Do we have your email, ma'am? Can we just send it via email?

07:59:28.990 --> 07:59:30.750
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: My subpoena was sent through email.

07:59:30.990 --> 07:59:31.390
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Okay.

07:59:32.070 --> 07:59:40.930
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Now... That would be all, ma'am. If there are no other interjections from the senator judges, we will excuse you.

07:59:42.680 --> 07:59:59.860
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Attorney Suzette, salamat po. Paumanhin, at least hindi kayo inabot ng pitong oras. 6 hours and 50 minutes lang. Salamat po sa inyong panahon, oras. At gayon din, pagsagot at pagtugon sa mga katanungan mula sa senator judges at mula sa magkabilang partido.

08:00:00.180 --> 08:00:01.600
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: You are excused, ma'am.

08:00:01.740 --> 08:00:02.460
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Thank you, Your Honor.

08:00:12.170 --> 08:00:45.780
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Before we excuse you, kindly consult your clients first. If you can submit it to us voluntarily, those two sets of documents. How it was booked and the return checks. Now, if you convey to us that you need a subpoena based on your discussions with your client, GenCorp, then we will issue the subpoena. But we will try to afford you the opportunity for us to do it from your end.

08:00:46.100 --> 08:00:46.940
Atty. Suzette Balucanag-Punay: Very well, Your Honor.

08:00:47.180 --> 08:00:48.060
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Atty. Sujet.

08:00:48.220 --> 08:00:48.660
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Before

08:01:02.580 --> 08:01:58.150
